WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Send ten tasks to your agents,

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.740
go to sleep, and wake up to the work

3
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:05.760
done, every step checked.

4
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.260
This is sequence three:

5
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:07.960
queues.

6
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.200
In this video: why a single agent

7
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.120
isn't enough, how the

8
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.680
inemaccbot queue works, and at the end,

9
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.220
the gate that stops the agent from

10
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.140
moving on without you.

11
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.840
An agent in the terminal does one thing

12
00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.420
at a time, and only while you're

13
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:19.880
watching.

14
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.760
If the internet drops or the machine

15
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.840
restarts, the work is lost.

16
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.500
And if you ask for ten things at the

17
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.080
same time, they trip over each other.

18
00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.700
To work on its own,

19
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:30.160
the agent needs a queue.

20
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.440
inemaccbot is a Telegram bot

21
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:33.400
with a durable queue.

22
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.800
Each request becomes a task stored in a

23
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:36.800
SQLite database.

24
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.420
The task is picked up with a heartbeat

25
00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:39.520
while it runs.

26
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.500
If it crashes, it goes back to the queue

27
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:42.280
and is resumed.

28
00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:43.400
Nothing is lost.

29
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.400
And what goes into the queue?

30
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.200
Skills that run as an agent:

31
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.260
transcribe, dub, explainer video,

32
00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:50.300
course, demo, reel.

33
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.880
You send the request through Telegram.

34
00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.440
The default engine is Claude Code,

35
00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.460
with Codex or OpenCode as an

36
00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:56.060
alternative.

37
00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:58.200
The next step is workflows:

38
00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.500
several phases in sequence,

39
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.120
with the state saved at each one.

40
00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.700
In the middle, a human gate.

41
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.700
The bot writes the texts and stops.

42
00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.820
You read them, and only when you approve does it

43
00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:07.920
move on to the avatar,

44
00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.700
the download, and the video.

45
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.400
Automatic, but with you in command.

46
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.740
This is where you stop being

47
00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:14.280
the one who does, and become the one who manages.

48
00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.440
You define the tasks,

49
00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:16.820
the gates, and the rules.

50
00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.300
The agents run them in the queue,

51
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.080
and you decide at the points that matter.

52
00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.000
With the queue up and running,

53
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.640
you can put social media on

54
00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.040
autopilot: sequence four.

55
00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:25.060
The

56
00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.120
inemaccbot, the guide, and the complete architecture

57
00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.920
are on INEMA dot CLUB,

58
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.420
open and free.

59
00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:31.820
Build your queue and send the

60
00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:32.660
first task.
